course: dictionary
lesson: 4505
title: Picture the word: haystack
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A haystack is a large pile of dried grass, called hay, kept outside on a farm. Farmers stack it up so the animals have food in winter, when grass does not grow. The word has two parts, hay and stack. A stack is a neat pile, so put them together and you can picture the meaning.
explain: Read this: «Sociable weavers build giant shared nests like haystacks in trees.» The words «like haystacks» tell you the nests have the same kind of heaped shape as a pile of hay. You can use the words around a new word as clues, just as you do with any other word.
explain: Haystack also appears in a saying: «like looking for a needle in a haystack». It means something is almost impossible to find, because a needle is tiny and hidden in all that hay. The words needle and looking are your clues.
fact: A haystack is a large pile of dried grass (hay) kept outside on a farm.
fact: Farmers keep hay to feed animals in winter, when grass does not grow well.
fact: Today hay is often rolled into round bales, but old stories and paintings still show haystacks.
fact: Claude Monet, a famous painter, made paintings of haystacks.
fact: Haystacks and hay bales can catch fire, so never play on them without permission.
exercise: Sociable weavers build giant shared nests «like haystacks in trees». What is a haystack? | A small flower that grows in fields | *A large pile of dried grass kept on a farm to feed animals in winter | A machine that cuts grass | A tall tree with thin branches
exercise: Someone says, «It's like looking for a needle in a haystack.» What does this mean? | Someone is sewing a quilt | Something is very easy to see | *Something is almost impossible to find | A farmer is cutting the hay
exercise: Find and copy the one word in «The farmer piled hay high in the yard» that tells you what the stack is made of. | yard | high | *hay | farmer
test: Why do farmers keep haystacks? | To build nests for birds | To make paintings for a gallery | To keep the grass wet | *To feed animals in winter
test: Why should children never play on haystacks? | Haystacks are made of sand | Haystacks always fall over in the wind | Haystacks are too soft to climb | *Haystacks and hay bales can catch fire
exam: Read: «Sociable weavers build giant shared nests like haystacks in trees.» What does haystack help you picture? | *A large rounded heap, like a pile of hay | A cold cave made of ice | A small blue egg | A wide flat river
